CHILD SAFETY STANDARDS

Last Updated: August 27, 2026

hiwee is committed to protecting children and maintaining a safe environment for all users. We have zero tolerance for child sexual abuse and exploitation (CSAE), including child sexual abuse material (CSAM).

1. PROHIBITED CONTENT AND CONDUCT

The following content and behavior are strictly prohibited on hiwee:

- Child sexual abuse material (CSAM).
- Sexual exploitation or abuse of children.
- Sexual solicitation or grooming of minors.
- Sexualized content involving children.
- Attempts to facilitate, promote, or encourage the exploitation of children.
- Any other conduct involving the sexual abuse or exploitation of children.

Users who violate these standards may have their content removed and their accounts suspended or permanently terminated.

2. REPORTING CHILD SAFETY CONCERNS

Users can report suspected child sexual abuse, exploitation, grooming, CSAM, or other child-safety concerns through the reporting functionality available within the app.

Users may also contact our child-safety team directly at:

Child Safety Contact:
joyaljoshy028@gmail.com

When submitting a report, users should provide as much relevant information as possible, such as the username, profile, message, content, or other information necessary to help us investigate the concern.

3. HANDLING REPORTS

We review child-safety reports and take appropriate action based on the circumstances and applicable laws.

Actions may include:

- Removing prohibited content.
- Restricting or disabling accounts.
- Permanently terminating accounts that violate our policies.
- Preserving relevant information where legally appropriate.
- Escalating serious matters to appropriate authorities when required by applicable law.

4. CSAM AND CHILD EXPLOITATION

hiwee does not permit CSAM or child sexual exploitation on its platform.

When we become aware of content or activity involving child sexual abuse or exploitation, we take appropriate action in accordance with our policies and applicable laws. Where legally required, confirmed CSAM or other relevant information will be reported to the appropriate authorities.

5. USER SAFETY

Users are encouraged to report any suspicious or inappropriate behavior involving children immediately.

Depending on the features available in the app, users may also have access to safety controls such as:

- Reporting users or content.
- Blocking users.
- Restricting unwanted interactions.
- Account and content moderation.

